                <pb facs="1052" n="1038" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.00/1664: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-30T15:00:00-04:00">May 30, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>464. Department approves stand which you have taken regarding asylum as reported
                    in your 522, May 29, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>As, however, an Associated Press despatch dated 3:45 a.m. May 30, Quito, reports
                    that Arroyo del Río has taken refuge in the American Embassy, the Department
                    would appreciate an urgent clarifying report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
